  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 916 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nSPC has portions of the area in a slight risk for severe weather \non Wednesday...mainly in the eastern half of the panhandles. The \nwestern low and trough will finally begin to move to the northeast \nand take on a bit of a negative tilt as it emerges into the western \nplains. Well defined boundaries to the north across southern KS and \nfrom a low in southeast CO through far western TX will be areas of \nfocus. At this time it seems as if the best chance for storms will \nbe near the KS/OK border and more scattered across the eastern \nthird of the panhandle. Since this time period is still a few days \naway more refinements are likely over the weekend. \n\nAs that system moves away from the area signs are pointing to a \ncold front that will be moving south across the area early Thursday \n(Oct 15). Temps will begin to fall with highs only in the 70s on \nThursday the 15th and then cooling into the 60's Friday.",
